    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0591" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72113/2218</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Peter</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23,
                        1928</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of January 17, 1928, in which you request, by instruction of your
                    Government, and with reference to the Treaty of November 25, 1850, between the
                    United States and Switzerland, the complete release of Swiss properties which
                    are still subjected to sequestration measures.</p>
                <p>In reply it gives me pleasure to inform you that a copy of your note under
                    acknowledgment has been transmitted to the Chairman of the Committee on Finance
                    of the Senate,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d326-f1"/> to which body there has been
                    referred an Act (H. R. 7201)<anchor n="4" xml:id="d326-f2"/> passed by the House
                    of Representatives on December 20, 1927, which contains <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >inter alia</hi> provisions for the disposition of property held by the
                    Alien Property Custodian.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. R.
                            Castle, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d326-f1" n="3" xml:id="d326-f1-content">
                <p>By letter of Jan. 23, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d326-f2" n="4" xml:id="d326-f2-content">
